style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001=
pt;mso-list:l1 level1 lfo2;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>The project recently updated =
its git hosting infrastructure and there were some issues encountered =
with the cgit http/https repository sharing. Those issues should now be =
resolved, apologies if they caused issues for anyone. The git:// =
protocol sharing was unaffected.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001=
pt;mso-list:l1 level1 lfo2;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>YP 3.0.2 rc2 is in QA with the =
report due soon.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001=
pt;mso-list:l1 level1 lfo2;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>We continue to see a small =
number of reproducibility issues with master which need resolving for =
green builds (in particular gstreamer and =
perl).<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001=
pt;mso-list:l1 level1 lfo2;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>A significant memory usage =
issue was identified during bitbake parsing where memory usage would =
grow in each parser thread linearly per number of recipes parsed. This =
would therefore particularly affect large numbers of layers, multilibs =
and multiconfig. The fix has merged into bitbake along with the =
corresponding zeus and warrior branches. For one test case it reduced =
peak memory usage during parsing for 5 multiconfigs from 20GB to =
2GB.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001=
pt;mso-list:l1 level1 lfo2;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>Warrior patches for 2.7.3 are =
out for review.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001=
pt;mso-list:l1 level1 lfo2;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>With the git infrastructure =
issue updated, we now have centos8 workers added to the =
autobuilder.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001=
pt;mso-list:l1 level1 lfo2;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>We are making various queued =
changes to the autobuilder configuration to fix bugs, improve efficiency =
and test coverage but this may result in some test result instability as =
we test and resolve issues.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001=
pt;mso-list:l1 level1 lfo2;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>We&#8217;re collecting a list =
of companies, products and projects which use the Yocto Project on the =
wiki: <a href=3D"https://wiki.yoctoproject.org/wiki/Project_Users"><span =
style=3D'color:#1155CC'>https://wiki.yoctoproject.org/wiki/Project_Users<=
/span></a> Please add any you know are missing (or email Richard/Stephen =
who can add).<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001=
pt;mso-list:l1 level1 lfo2;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>The triage team is worried =
